  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacity of Specialized Criminal Justice and Law Enforcement institutions and Officials to Respond Effectively to Emerging threats</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From 2022 - 2025 Niger experienced a huge increase in terrorism related deaths. Since the coup in 2023, the presence of several military assistant forces terminated, Niger withdrew from ECOWAS, groups established stronger presence in Tillaberi amongst others. Escalating terrorist threats, the outbreak in the Koutoukale prison in 2024, increased the security gap and stretched the armed forces between protecting the transition government and terrorist attacks in the west. Also, rotation of personnel in the specialized law enforcement institutions led to an increase of backlog of terrorism/organized crime cases, prison overcrowding, unjustified prolongment of pretrial detention related to alleged terrorism and criminal acts. There is urgent need to improve capacity to process cases related to T&amp;OC, strengthen capacity of criminal justice officials, data collection, criminal justice response to counter the nexus between T&amp;OC, foster community engagement in preventing and countering T&amp;OC.</narrative>
  </description>
